    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nMini.files\n\n### Description\n\nWhen I open Mini.Files, and close the window, reopening mini.files gives an error and causes mini.files to stop working.\r\n\r\nI have simple mini.files config, and one keymap for it.\r\n```lua\r\n  require(\"mini.files\").setup({\r\n    mappings = {\r\n      go_in_plus = \"<cr>\",\r\n      synchronize = \"<c-s>\",\r\n    },\r\n    windows = {\r\n      max_number = 3,\r\n      preview = true,\r\n    },\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  vim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"-\", function()\r\n    MiniFiles.open(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0))\r\n    MiniFiles.reveal_cwd()\r\n  end, { desc = \"Open Mini Files\" })\r\n```\r\n\r\nSome other things I observed.\r\n1. After Mini.files crashes, the \"-\" keybind stops working.\r\n2. If I navigate to some other files, Using Mini.Pick or Arrow.nvim, and press \"-\" again. Mini.Files opens, but closing that window and reopening it again give me the same error\r\n3. If I replace the `MiniFiles.Open()` call with `MiniFiles.open(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0), false)` like given in the readme, to open a \"fresh\" window, that makes everything work as expected, and I can close and reopen MiniFiles as many times as I want.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.10.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. Press \"-\" to open Mini.Files window\r\n3. Press q to exit the window\r\n4. Press \"-\" to open Mini.files window again\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nReopen the Mini.Files window again...\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nI receive this error\r\n```\r\nError executing vim.schedule lua callback: ...e/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2378: attempt to compare number with nil\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        ...e/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2378: in function 'is_modified_buffer'\r\n        ...e/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2550: in function 'window_update_border_hl'\r\n        ...e/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2519: in function 'window_set_view'\r\n        ...e/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:1779: in function 'explorer_refresh_depth_window'\r\n        ...e/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:1505: in function 'explorer_refresh'\r\n        ...e/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:778: in function 'open'\r\n        /home/sumit/.config/nvim/lua/plugins/mini.lua:61: in function </home/sumit/.config/nvim/lua/plugins/mini.lua:60>\r\n```",
