            "body": "Actually, My MiniJump2D is also a bit broken for the past few days, I didn't bother trying to fix that(Or thought anything of it when I noticed), Since I don't use it that much. But That's also not occurring with the minimal.lua example.\r\n\r\nIn case of MiniJump2D, I have to press the \"label letters\" sequence twice to jump to the place I want. For example,\r\n1. I press <Enter> to start MiniJump2D\r\n2. Press, let's say \"r' and then \"w\" labels\r\n3. after pressing \"w\", the label resets to original un-filtered labels, And I have to press \"r\" and \"w\" again to jump.",
