        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> So I don't know what the issue might be.\r\n\r\nMy guess would be to start with the following:\r\n- Execute `:nmap q` when inside 'mini.files' buffer. Maybe it gets defined to do something else.\r\n- Try disabling plugins which might interact with floating windows or key presses (like 'folke/which-key.nvim').\r\n- Fully bisect config.\r\n\r\n> Actually, My MiniJump2D is also a bit broken for the past few days, I didn't bother trying to fix that(Or thought anything of it when I noticed), Since I don't use it that much. But That's also not occurring with the minimal.lua example.\r\n\r\nThen I am afraid it is definitely some third party plugin (or you config function/autocommand) behaving in conflicting manner.\r\n\r\nClosing as not an issue with 'mini.nvim' per se. If you find a reproducible example which uses only it, please let me know.",
